+## HTTPS
+
+Set `server.protocol` to `https` and provide a certificate and its matching private key. Flipt validates that both files exist and loads the key pair before starting either listener. The REST API and UI use `server.https_port`; gRPC continues to use `server.grpc_port` and also serves TLS. The certificate must contain a DNS or IP subject alternative name for the REST gateway's connection to gRPC.
+
+```yaml
+server:
+  protocol: https
+  https_port: 443
+  grpc_port: 9000
+  cert_file: /etc/flipt/tls/cert.pem
+  cert_key: /etc/flipt/tls/key.pem
+```
+
+The same settings can be supplied with `FLIPT_SERVER_PROTOCOL`, `FLIPT_SERVER_HTTPS_PORT`, `FLIPT_SERVER_CERT_FILE`, and `FLIPT_SERVER_CERT_KEY`.
+
 ## Databases
 
 Flipt supports both [SQLite](https://www.sqlite.org/index.html) and [Postgres](https://www.postgresql.org/) databases as of `v0.5.0`.
